.TH BLUESENTRY 1 "September 2026" "BlueSentry 1.0.0" "System Maintenance & Security Tools"
.SH NAME
bluesentry \- Advanced Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) passive scanner, analyzer, and signal tracker

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bluesentry
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIduration\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput_file\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B BlueSentry
is a high-performance passive Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) reconnaissance, auditing, and telemetry application. It operates by capturing over-the-air BLE advertising packets (GAP broadcasts) without pairing or active transmission.
.PP
The application extracts payload telemetry including IEEE MAC address privacy flags, proprietary vendor protocol headers (such as Apple Continuity and AirDrop), and Received Signal Strength Indicator (RSSI) proximity metrics.
.PP
In addition to live passive surveillance, BlueSentry includes an interactive GATT interrogator and a targeted signal tracker (\fIBloodhound\fR) equipped with Exponential Moving Average (EMA) signal stabilization.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-duration " \fIseconds\fR"
Defines the duration of the scan phase in seconds. Defaults to \fB20\fR seconds.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfilename\fR"
Specifies the destination CSV file for telemetry logging. If unspecified, the application automatically outputs to \fIsentry_log_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.csv\fR in the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-passive
Executes in headless/passive surveillance mode. Suppresses the interactive Rich TUI and post-scan menu; streams output directly to disk. Suitable for 24/7 background daemons.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Outputs command syntax, argument flags, and operational examples, then exits.

.SH OPERATIONAL MODES

.SS Live Terminal Dashboard (TUI)
When executed interactively without \fB\-p\fR, BlueSentry renders a split-screen dashboard:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTop Pane:\fR Real-time tabular feed sorted dynamically by RSSI power. Columns display Target ID, Hardware Address, Privacy Bit (RAND/PUB), RSSI (dBm), Resolved Vendor Name, and GATT Services.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBottom Pane:\fR ASCII radial proximity radar visualizing target distance relative to the host receiver antenna.

.SS Device Interrogation
Connects asynchronously to a target peripheral, walks the GATT Service hierarchy, and reads exposed public characteristics (Device Name, Battery Percentage, Hardware Revision) without requiring pairing.

.SS Bloodhound Signal Tracker
Locks onto a designated BD_ADDR and renders an ASCII live signal power trend using \fBplotext\fR. Applies Exponential Moving Average (EMA, alpha = 0.35) filtering to eliminate multipath radio spikes.

.SH PERMISSIONS AND CAPABILITIES
Under Linux, raw BLE socket access traditionally requires superuser privileges. Running BlueSentry under \fBsudo\fR is strongly discouraged in production environments.
.PP
To permit non-root execution, assign Linux capabilities to your Python binary:
.PP
.nf
.RS
# setcap 'cap_net_raw,cap_net_admin+eip' $(readlink \-f $(which python3))
.RE
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I sentry_log_*.csv
Default CSV output files generated automatically at the termination of each scan session.

